NNAAMMEE
     ccttffdduummpp — dump the SUNW_ctf section of an ELF file

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ccttffdduummpp [--ddffhhllssSStt] --uu _f_i_l_e file

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccttffdduummpp utility dumps the contents of the CTF (Compact C Type Format)
     data section (SUNW_ctf) present in an ELF binary file.  This section was
     previously created with ctfconvert(1) or ctfmerge(1).

     The following options are available:

     --dd      Show the data object section.

     --ff      Show the function section.

     --hh      Show the header.

     --ll      Show the label section.

     --ss      Show the string table.

     --SS      Show statistics.

     --tt      Show the type section.

     --uu _u_f_i_l_e
             Write the uncompressed CTF data to a raw CTF file called _u_f_i_l_e.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ccttffdduummpp utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ctfconvert(1), ctfmerge(1), ctf(5)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ccttffdduummpp utility first appeared in FreeBSD 7.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The CTF utilities came from OpenSolaris.

